mode: "100644"
text: "# Post Brief — the unit the content skills execute\n\nThe plan's value is that every slot is a **brief**, not a vague idea. A brief is specific enough\nthat `caption-writer`, `reels-script`, or any content skill can turn it into a finished,\non-voice post with no further conversation. \"Post about productivity, Tuesday\" is not a brief.\n\n## The brief schema\n\nEach calendar slot carries:\n\n```\n- date / time (+ timezone)      when it goes out\n- platform(s)                   where (and per-platform variants if fanning out)\n- pillar                        which theme it belongs to\n- goal / intent                 educate / entertain / inspire / connect / promote (+ the metric)\n- format                        carousel / Reel / single image / text / thread / story\n- hook angle                    the opening direction (drafted via hook-writer)\n- core idea                     the one point or story the post makes\n- CTA                           the single action (matched to goal + platform)\n- asset / creative tool         photo needed? video via Veo? graphic via Nano Banana? none?\n- repurposed from               source idea, if adapted from another post\n- status                        planned → drafted → approved → scheduled\n```\n\nA good brief answers \"what is this post, exactly?\" — not \"what topic is it near?\"\n\n## How content skills execute a brief\n\nThe plan is the spine; the content skills fill it:\n\n1. `hook-writer` → sharpens the **hook angle** into the actual opening (for the format).\n2. `caption-writer` / `reels-script` / `thread-writer` → writes the finished post from the\n   brief, in the brand voice, hitting the goal and CTA.\n3. Creative-tool mini-skills (`veo-3`, `nano-banana`, …) → produce any **asset** the brief\n   calls for.\n4. `scheduling-and-queue` → schedules the approved post at the brief's date/time.\n\nBecause the brief already fixes goal, format, hook angle, and CTA, the content skill isn't\nguessing — it's executing. That's what makes a batch fast *and* consistent.\n\n## Brief quality checklist\n\nA slot is ready when:\n\n- [ ] It names **one** clear idea and **one** goal.\n- [ ] The **format** suits the idea and platform.\n- [ ] There's a real **hook angle**, not just a topic.\n- [ ] The **CTA** matches the goal and the platform's mechanics.\n- [ ] Any **asset/tool** dependency is flagged (so production isn't blocked later).\n- [ ] It inherits the brand's **voice and guardrails**.\n\n## Level of detail\n\nDefault: write the **brief** for every slot, plus fully draft a few exemplars so the user can\nsee the voice and approve the direction. Write *all* the final copy only if asked — otherwise\nthe content skills do that, on demand, from the briefs. This keeps planning fast and avoids\nproducing a month of copy the user may want to reshuffle first.\n"
